%9Setting:%9

    sidepanel_left_width (number; default: 15, the Shellter default
    configuration sets 20)

%9Description:%9

    The width in columns of the left side panel (the window list), its border
    included.

    A panel is at least 6 columns wide: a smaller number is taken as 6.
    0 hides the panel, as /SET sidepanel_left OFF does. The panels
    give way to the main windows: a panel is shown only while the
    terminal has room for it next to the widest row of main windows (20
    columns for each window), so it can go and come back as the terminal
    is resized or windows are split side by side.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET sidepanel_left_width 20
    /SET sidepanel_left off

%9See also:%9

    SET, SIDEPANEL_RIGHT_WIDTH, WINDOW

